  "details": "A strong UX improvement would be a host-level toggle to hide avatars under a certain performance tier. Since avatar stats are already tracked, this would encourage optimization without limiting creativity—much like age verification improved safety.\n\nPerformance remains one of the most critical vulnerabilities in VRChat up to date! \n\nCurrently, avatar performance is treated as a personal responsibility. We users are expected to choose optimized avatars or manually hide others. However, this approach is reactive and inconsistent, especially in public or friends lobbies. Since ppl are aware but don't care enough. YET \n\nSo this change would shift the awareness to a Community demand! \n\nBy introducing this relativly simple change we would do the following:\n\n1. Empower community organizers (event hosts, world creators) to enforce performance standards in real-time, without moderation overhead. VERY DESIRED, same as with Age-Verification. Making Events more easy to host and maintain.\n\n2. Create a culture of performance awareness, making optimization not just a niche priority but a baseline expectation for public engagement. This also encourage Avatar-Creatores to put more time into Avatar optimization since this change creates a demand for it.\n\n3. Make this enforcement optional, giving hosts flexibility while protecting creative freedom for more relaxed or experimental Avatars. It simply introduces a new Standard, not forces it!",
